2. Project Title & System Concept
Project Title

Smart Clinic Management & Patient Flow Optimization System

System Description

The Smart Clinic Management System is a unified desktop application designed to manage patient records, appointments, emergency handling, and clinic navigation efficiently.

The system emphasizes custom Data Structures and Algorithms (DSAs) to achieve optimized performance and structured data handling.

All modules operate as one integrated system, not as separate mini-projects.

Technology Stack

Java (Swing)

Graphical User Interface

User interaction & input validation

Result visualization

C++

Core Data Structures & Algorithms

No inbuilt DSA libraries used

JSON (File-Based Communication)

Java ↔ C++ integration

3. Module Design

The system consists of two fully integrated modules.

MODULE 1: Patient Records & Appointment Management
(A) C++ Component – DSA & Algorithm Logic
Level-1 Data Structures
1. Arrays

Purpose: Temporary storage of raw patient input

Operations:

Insert

Index-based access

Benefits:

Fast access

Structured preprocessing before advanced DSAs

2. Linked List

Purpose: Dynamic storage of patient records

Operations:

Insert patient

Delete patient

Search patient

Traverse records

Benefits:

Dynamic memory usage

Efficient insertion and deletion

Level-2 Data Structures
1. AVL Tree (Balanced BST)

Purpose: Store patient records sorted by Patient ID

Operations:

Insert

Delete

Search

Tree rotations (LL, RR, LR, RL)

Benefits:

Automatic balancing

O(log n) time complexity

Faster than linear searching

(B) Java GUI Component

Framework: Java Swing

Interface Style: Single window with tab-based layout

Input Fields

Patient ID

Patient Name

Age

Disease

Appointment Date

Actions

Add Patient

Delete Patient

Search Patient

View All Patients

Output & Visualization

Patient records in tables / text areas

Status messages using dialog boxes

Validation & Error Handling

Empty input validation

Numeric ID validation

Duplicate patient detection

File read/write error handling

The GUI clearly reflects how DSAs process and store data.

(C) Integration Layer (Java ↔ C++)

Integration Method: File-based JSON communication

Data Flow

Java GUI collects user input

Data written to patient_input.json

C++ backend manually parses JSON

DSAs process data

Output written to patient_output.json

Java reads output and displays results

This approach ensures simplicity, reliability, and clear separation between frontend and backend.

(D) Work Allocation – Module 1
