MODULE 2: Emergency Queue & Clinic Navigation
(A) C++ Component – DSA & Algorithm Logic
Level-1 Data Structures
1. Queue

Purpose: Normal patient flow

Operations: Enqueue, Dequeue

Benefit: First-come, first-serve processing

2. Stack

Purpose: Undo last emergency operation (simulation)

Operations: Push, Pop

Benefit: Efficient tracking of recent actions

Level-2 Data Structures
1. Heap / Priority Queue

Purpose: Manage emergency patients by severity

Operations:

Insert with priority

Extract highest priority

Heapify

Benefits:

Critical patients treated first

O(log n) performance

2. Graph (BFS Traversal)

Purpose: Model clinic layout (rooms, labs, pharmacy)

Operations:

BFS traversal

Shortest path discovery

Benefits:

Efficient navigation

Real-world clinic modeling

(B) Java GUI Component
Input Fields

Patient Name

Severity Level (1–10)

Starting Room

Destination Room

Actions

Add Emergency Patient

Process Next Patient

Show Shortest Clinic Route

Output

Priority queue order

Route displayed in textual form

Error Handling

Invalid severity values

Incorrect or missing room names

Empty data handling

(C) Integration Layer

Same JSON-based communication for consistency

Files Used:

emergency_input.json

emergency_output.json

